            },
            "after": {
              "kind": "modifier_constant",
              "where": "budget_measures/zero_vat_on_domestic_electricity.py zero_vat_on_domestic_electricity(rate_change_2026, rate_change_2027), rate_change_2026 divided by that module's WINTER_SHARE (the October to March share of a year's electricity use) and rate_change_2027 by its SPRING_SHARE (the April to June share), October 2026 to June 2027 (the dates in the measure's description)"
            }
          },
          "card_note": "0% instead of 5% in Great Britain from 1 October 2026. The Budget expects the zero rate to apply in Northern Ireland too from 1 April 2027, and the model counts it there from then. The October to March zero rate was already law (SI 2026/987); like the Treasury's costing, the model scores the whole period against 5%."
